  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-{sec}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$",
